<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73491" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρο-πάτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who
				tramples on Homer,</i> epith. of Xenophanes in Timo <i><span class="en">
				60.1
			</span></i> as quoted by <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.18
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-απάτης</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.224
			</span></i>, which may be nom. masc., <i>perverter of Homer,</i> or
			gen. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηραπάτη,</span>
			<i>the Homeric fiction,</i> as expld. by <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
